what is terraform
terraform is a tool used to create and manage infrastructure using code
instead of creating resources manually on cloud we write code and terraform creates it

created by HashiCorp

why we use terraform
automation no manual work
fast deployment
reusable code
version control with github
works with multiple cloud providers

what is infrastructure as code
writing infrastructure in code form
example instead of creating ec2 manually we write code and terraform creates it

how terraform works

1 write code
2 terraform init
3 terraform plan
4 terraform apply

terraform commands

terraform init
initialize project download plugins

terraform plan
shows what will be created

terraform apply
creates resources

terraform destroy
deletes resources

what is provider

provider means cloud service

example

provider "aws" {
region = "ap-south-1"
}

tells terraform to use aws and region

what is resource

resource means actual service we create

example

resource "aws_instance" "my_ec2" {
ami = "ami-xxxx"
instance_type = "t2.micro"
}

this creates ec2 instance

basic structure

provider define cloud
resource create service

what is state file

terraform.tfstate

stores
what resources created
their ids

very important file

problem with local state

stored in laptop
not safe
team cannot use
can be lost

what is backend

backend is place where terraform stores state file

s3 backend

stores state in cloud

example

terraform {
backend "s3" {
bucket = "my-bucket"
key = "dev/terraform.tfstate"
region = "ap-south-1"
}
}

what is dynamodb

used for locking

prevents multiple users running terraform at same time

backend with dynamodb

terraform → s3 store state
terraform → dynamodb lock

what is variable

used to make code dynamic

example

variable "instance_type" {}

use

instance_type = var.instance_type

what is output

used to display result

example

output "ip" {
value = aws_instance.my_ec2.public_ip
}

what is module

module means reusable code

example ec2 module s3 module

used in big projects

